WEBVTT

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.480
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:47.960
<b>Season of Warmth</b>

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.980
Come on, hurry up!

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.190
Gintaro, did Haru-chan come back?

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.650
No, he didn't.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:57.770
See? What do we do now?

00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.080
Let go of my arm.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.400
I won't run away.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.610
Oh, sorry.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:06.150
Hey, you know that heralds will 
disappear if they're away

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.010
from their shrine too long, right?

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:13.140
I told you that kid would be trouble.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:19.510
He's clearly "in too 
deep" for a herald.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.700
I'm sorry.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.660
I had a feeling this might happen.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:28.310
Haru is a relatively young herald.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:34.110
There's another herald at our shrine.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.860
Haru should not have left him behind.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:41.200
That kid isn't the only one 
who left someone behind.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:44.310
W-Well...

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:49.830
Don't you get tired 
of being so uptight?

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.040
You need to learn to take it easy.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:56.880
This girl's an heir to a shrine,
 yet look at her.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.240
Wait, what?

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.810
Heralds have their own minds.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:02.630
They do what they want.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:07.270
If they get sick of it 
all, they'll leave.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.960
That's happened before...

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.350
So if the kid wants out, let him go.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:18.570
Don't make the kid my responsibility.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:23.610
Hey, there!

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:29.540
What? Another fox spirit?

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.980
And that's the only surprise?

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:33.530
You can really see them?

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:36.990
No wonder you kids hit it off so quick.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.500
I see how it is.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.290
I'm the only one who can't see them.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:43.190
I feel so alone.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:46.470
Sorry about this.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:49.150
I'm thrilled about the 
new family member,

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:53.700
so why do the two of you 
look like someone died?

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:59.270
Oh, is that what Gintaro-sama said?

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:03.570
Yeah. Gin doesn't seem 
to like Haru-chan.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.130
He doesn't want the responsibility.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.820
Our doors are open.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:13.540
No, I believe that I'm the one 
Gintaro-sama is upset with.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:18.110
In any case, I'll be sending Haru back.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:21.500
I apologize for the 
trouble I've caused.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.340
Can you stop doing that?!

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.870
We need to worry 
about finding Haru-chan

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.690
before talking about 
sending anyone back!

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.070
Now, now, Makoto.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:29.260
Sit down.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:33.920
Your father and I went 
to the same college.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:38.210
I never got to meet him, 
but we had the same teacher.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.500
Tahara-sensei...

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:44.210
Yes, I believe he was friends 
with your grandfather.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:47.950
Yes, he's been helping me out.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.820
I recall that your family's shrine

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:53.460
has been around for 
about 1,200 years, right?

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:56.660
Your aunt and uncle are 
running it right now.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:05.090
Ah. If you can see Haru-sama, 
you must be the successor.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.320
When did you inherit the Sight?

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.870
I was four.

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:11.300
I was... five.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:14.770
Satoru,

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:20.230
this is an Inari shrine, which 
means there are fox spirits around.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:21.940
Where?

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.150
You'll meet them soon.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:29.750
Don't worry. I'll keep you safe.

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:35.530
Father...

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:39.410
It's only been two years since 
my brother's accident...

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:41.740
He was pushing himself too hard.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.580
Satoru-kun, there's 
nothing to worry about.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.780
We'll take care of everything.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:10.200
He has the same eyes as my brother 
that I could never stand!

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:12.240
Don't say that.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.440
Honestly, why did Father 
have to leave a will?

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:18.160
We're the ones managing the shrine.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.800
It only makes sense for one of our 
children to inherit the shrine!

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.260
Hey, Sayaka. You're too loud.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.870
Satoru-kun.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:34.600
Y-Yes.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:40.180
I decided to take you in because 
it was a request from my teacher.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.190
However, you seem a little 
too responsible for someone

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:44.850
the same age as Makoto.

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:47.320
It's rather unfortunate.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:51.030
Yes, it's unfortunate.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:59.240
If you'd like, you're free to 
consider this shrine your new home.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:04.250
Or something like that. 
Sorry, I can be a bit meddlesome at times.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:10.340
Now, don't you need to 
go look for Haru-sama?

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:15.220
But Gin said to leave Haru-chan alone.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.380
He doesn't want the responsibility.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:26.270
You know how you always say that 
Gintaro likes to be contrary?

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:31.150
That sounds exactly like 
something he would say.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:38.080
Does he mean that they should 
figure it out themselves?

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:42.040
Yes, I'm guessing that 
Gintaro-sama's point is that

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:46.990
it comes down to whether Satoru-kun 
wants to be with Haru-sama or not.

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:48.000
It's that simple.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:52.660
Fortunately, our shrine 
is also an Inari shrine,

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:56.340
so you have the option to 
be together right now.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:02.840
It hurts to be separated when 
you most want to be together.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.400
W-Wait, Satoru-kun?!

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.590
I'm leaving.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:14.190
Where are you going?

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:17.660
Satoru, I'm coming with you!

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.180
You can't.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:22.230
I wanna be with you!

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.510
You are the fox spirit here.

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:26.620
You need to stay here in my place.

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:30.500
I'm not going to succeed the shrine.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:32.590
I'll live on my own.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.670
Satoru...

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:37.970
I'm sorry, Haru!

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:41.060
Hold on. You won't find Haru-chan 
by running around by yourself.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.180
This is all my fault!

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:44.520
I'll find Haru by myself!

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.300
Let's ask Gin, then.

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:52.020
Gintaro can divine where 
people and objects are.

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:54.150
Satoru-kun!

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:57.040
Just leave them alone, you nosy idiot.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:57.860
What?!

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:02.650
Like I said, heralds 
have their own issues.

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:05.580
Humans are no different, right?

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:07.710
I guess...

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.670
Then let them be.

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:14.630
Besides, you should probably be 
here when that kid comes back,

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:20.340
since I'm staying out of this business.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.550
Huh?

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.980
Wait, Gin!

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.890
Come on, Gin!

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.230
Jeez!

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.980
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.900
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:37.650
Haru-sama! Haru-sama!

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.700
Oh, you're outside.

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:47.120
Have a look. My grandson just 
left the hospital today.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:50.460
He's so small!

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:53.170
It wasn't so long ago that 
you were just as small.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.590
Please have mercy.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.860
So this is your grandson.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:01.030
We've named him Satoru.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:03.180
He will be the 77th successor.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.400
Satoru...

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.810
Look, Togo! Satoru can see me!

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.600
No, he can't see you yet.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:14.130
He's looking right at me!

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:16.530
So you're Satoru...

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.030
Satoru...

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.530
Satoru...

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.790
<i>They still aren't back...</i>

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.360
<i>Should I go look for them?</i>

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.910
You didn't find Haru-chan?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:55.550
I thought I could live on my own now,

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:58.030
but I can't do anything.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:11:59.470
Then ask Gin for help.

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:02.730
I'm already imposing on 
you and Tatsuo-san.

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:05.570
I can't ask Gintaro-sama 
for more help.

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:11.170
It's all because I'm just a child...

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:12.840
How stupid are you?!

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:14.990
It doesn't matter if 
you're a child or not!

00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:17.040
What matters is that you're human!

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:21.170
Nobody can live on their own!

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.430
What's wrong with asking 
the gods for help?!

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:24.640
Gin!

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.010
Look for Haru-chan!

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:29.700
Stop pretending to be asleep!

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:35.100
You know, you're not asking the 
gods for help. You're asking me.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:36.690
Just do it!

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:41.290
Hey, you need to learn how 
to restrain yourself.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.410
Please help.

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.610
I knew deep down that I couldn't 
do anything on my own.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:49.910
I was running away from that fact.

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:53.620
If we have to be separated, 
separating sooner

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.460
wouldn't be as painful for Haru...

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:58.790
No, I thought it wouldn't 
be as painful for me.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.370
Haru's always been there for me.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:05.890
Haru even followed me here.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.550
I was happy to have Haru here.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:16.640
If possible, I want to 
spend more time with Haru!

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:23.840
Heh, you've opened up quite a bit.

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:27.110
Damn, guess I can't refuse, then.

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:35.410
I've never searched 
for a herald before,

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.760
so I don't know if this will work.

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:08.700
It's a goner.

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:15.940
Make sure you clean yourself off.

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:18.300
Foxes can carry disease.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:23.500
I will hold a memorial for it.

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:27.480
But it's not your fox, is it?

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.550
I live in an Inari shrine.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.840
<b>Kamio Shrine</b>

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:24.230
Oh, you must be that fox.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.190
It appears that you've become a herald.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.050
A herald?

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:34.910
Oh, dear. It appears that 
Seigo brought you here.

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:40.620
My partner passed away last month.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:43.690
And soon after, a new one arrives.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:45.590
Funny how things work out.

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:49.680
What's he doing?

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:52.550
He's making a grave for you.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:56.810
It's a cherry blossom tree.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:16:00.860
Come spring, it'll be in full bloom.

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:02.700
What's spring?

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.720
A season of warmth.

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:07.570
Warmth...

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:13.950
My name is Otomatsu.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.340
What's yours?

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.240
Ah...

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:21.440
That boy will inherit this shrine.

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:23.790
He can't see us right now,

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.210
but he will some day.

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:29.430
When the time comes,

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.580
you should call yourself Haru (spring).

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:36.470
Haru...

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:50.280
Togo, don't go.

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:54.790
Otomatsu-sama. Haru-sama.

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:58.160
Once I'm gone,

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:00.870
please take care of the shrine...

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:05.190
Please take care of Satoru.

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:26.190
Satoru.

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:29.400
I'm Haru.

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:32.090
Haru?

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:35.620
Can you make up your mind?

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:38.070
It's not that simple...

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:01.100
Satoru, don't be sad.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:02.940
I'm here for you.

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:15.610
Am I going to disappear?

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:21.150
I guess it doesn't matter if 
I can't be with Satoru...

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:27.460
Togo, I'm sorry I couldn't 
keep my promise.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:29.540
Haru!

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:39.720
Haru.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.930
Sa-Sa—

00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:49.060
Satoru, sorry about bothering you.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:51.590
So I'll just...

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:52.900
You're not...

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:56.230
You're not bothering... me.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:02.620
Haru...

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:05.340
I'm... sorry.

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:12.170
Satoru!

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.490
I'm sorry about saying those things!

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:26.400
We did the right thing.

00:19:26.400 --> 00:19:29.640
Hmm? Where's your

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:31.890
"Aw, isn't it so beautiful?"

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:33.570
reaction?

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.780
When did I ever do that?

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:37.360
I'm not sure.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:39.320
I mean...

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:44.330
He's clearly "in too 
deep" for a herald.

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:47.760
They can't be together forever...

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:52.120
Why worry about the future?

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:56.300
You're the one doing as you please 
and living in the moment.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:57.840
Gin...

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:01.730
They still have some growing 
up to do, as do you.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:05.050
Wait a few years and 
they'll find an answer.

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:11.090
Right.

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:13.600
Then it's okay for now.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.580
For now...

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:22.610
Man, I was getting a little worried.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.900
This is wonderful news.

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:29.300
Then let's celebrate our new family!

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:31.170
It's a pleasure...

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:32.580
Glad to have you...

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:37.450
So, Haru-chan?

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.660
Where's Haru-chan?

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:40.380
Over here?

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:42.510
Or over there?

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.190
Oh, I shouldn't say Haru-chan.

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:46.470
Haru-sama would be more appropriate.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:50.680
Well, you'd use Haru-chan 
if you could see.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:52.640
What's that mean?!

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:56.760
Sorry, I should stop 
calling you Haru-chan.

00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:58.610
How about Haru-kun?

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:04.780
I'm a girl!

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:06.240
What?!

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.830
I don't believe this!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:09.050
I'm sorry!

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:11.510
This is outrageous!

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:14.680
I haven't seen Haru having 
this much fun before.

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:18.920
What about you?

00:21:26.730 --> 00:21:29.350
We won't leave you alone Otomatsu-sama.

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:31.930
I'll talk to Haru.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:35.420
Oh, don't worry about me.

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:37.100
Haru is still young.

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:39.650
She should go out and see the world.

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:42.510
I'm old now.

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:46.010
I'll stay and see what 
happens to this shrine.

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:49.000
And the people who can't see me.

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:54.560
Satoru, you are very similar to Seigo.

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:56.080
My great-grandfather?

00:21:56.870 --> 00:22:02.050
That's probably why Haru 
thinks of you as...

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:05.310
Well, it's not important.

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:09.550
<i>Take it easy, Satoru.</i>

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:12.810
Satoru, this girl's a lost cause!

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:13.610
What?

00:22:13.610 --> 00:22:16.660
My name is Makoto!

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:19.560
Take it easy...

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:29.980
Hey, girl!

00:22:29.980 --> 00:22:31.810
Don't stare at Satoru!

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:32.550
What? What?

00:22:32.550 --> 00:22:34.910
Man, it's so noisy...

00:22:34.910 --> 00:22:36.910
You both have school tomorrow.

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:38.460
Thank you for everything.

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:19.520
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:19.520
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:24:11.410 --> 00:24:13.480
Heralds are messengers
 from the gods...

00:24:13.480 --> 00:24:15.100
Hey, girl!

00:24:15.100 --> 00:24:17.740
You know nothing about heralds!

00:24:17.740 --> 00:24:19.520
S-Sorry, Haru-chan!

00:24:19.560 --> 00:25:00.000
<b>How Do I Look?</b>

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:22.470
Next time: How Do I Look?

00:24:22.470 --> 00:24:25.190
May fortune be with you.
